WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.872 --> 00:00:15.153
aren't we going to the hippodrome?"

2
00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:18.996
Julia asked Hermes as the group entered the gymnasium the next day.

3
00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:23.839
"I thought you'd want Brody to work on his chariot driving some more."

4
00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:27.301
"That can wait," Hermes replied.

5
00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:31.004
"I've had enough of watching chariot driving for a while.

6
00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:37.686
Besides, if I ask Poseidon to borrow his horses again so soon, he'll think I'm worried about Brody's

7
00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:38.767
chances in the event."

8
00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:41.148
Julia didn't respond.

9
00:00:42.849 --> 00:00:48.171
She was pretty sure Poseidon had already figured out that Brody wasn't an expert chariot driver!

10
00:00:49.131 --> 00:00:52.613
Athena and her champion spotted Hermes and Brody and came over.

11
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:59.236
"My champion is training for the hoplitodromos," Athena told Hermes.

12
00:01:00.448 --> 00:01:03.969
"We've reached the point where he would benefit from running against an opponent.

13
00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:05.330
Can we train with you?"

14
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.030
"The hoplitodromos."

15
00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:10.071
Hermes snapped his fingers.

16
00:01:10.091 --> 00:01:12.432
"I knew there was something I meant to do today!"

17
00:01:12.452 --> 00:01:16.593
"The hoplitodromos," Julia said to Markos.

18
00:01:17.653 --> 00:01:19.974
"That's the race where the runners have to wear armor, right?"

19
00:01:19.994 --> 00:01:22.775
"Yes," Markos said.

20
00:01:22.795 --> 00:01:26.016
"It's quite a test of an athlete's strength and endurance."

21
00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:32.516
Julia watched as Hermes snapped his fingers again and a pile of metal armor fell out of the

22
00:01:32.576 --> 00:01:33.737
sky with a clang.

23
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.424
It was so loud that it startled Ares, who instantly turned into a huge, growling dog.

24
00:01:41.444 --> 00:01:45.707
"Sorry, my friend," Hermes called out with a smirk.

25
00:01:45.727 --> 00:01:47.369
"I didn't mean to scare you."

26
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.432
Ares returned to his normal form and scowled at Hermes.

27
00:01:51.452 --> 00:01:55.676
"You didn't scare me, messenger," he snapped.

28
00:01:56.212 --> 00:01:57.653
"You merely distracted me!"

29
00:01:59.034 --> 00:02:03.738
Julia watched Ares grab his champion and drag him off toward the javelin area.

30
00:02:04.779 --> 00:02:06.661
She was glad to see the war god go.

31
00:02:08.762 --> 00:02:12.986
After his trick with the javelins, Ares made Julia nervous when he was close.

32
00:02:13.006 --> 00:02:20.152
"I guess it's a good thing Brody gets to practice with Athena's champion," Julia said.

33
00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:25.276
"Athena probably won't turn Brody's shield into a hungry wolf or something."

34
00:02:26.328 --> 00:02:27.289
Markos chuckled.

35
00:02:27.309 --> 00:02:33.091
"True. It's too bad we can't say the same for most of the other gods.

36
00:02:34.331 --> 00:02:38.633
I hear they're already coming up with ways to sabotage Alcides as soon as he arrives."

37
00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.375
Julia noticed Hermes staring at them.

38
00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.716
"Well?" the god said.

39
00:02:45.736 --> 00:02:50.358
"Are you just going to sit there, or are you going to help my champion get ready?"

40
00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:52.559
"Sorry, Hermes."

41
00:02:53.179 --> 00:02:54.900
Markos scurried over to Brody.

42
00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.361
Julia went to help too.

43
00:02:58.961 --> 00:03:04.664
The armor consisted of a metal helmet, a large wooden shield covered in bronze, and a pair of

44
00:03:04.744 --> 00:03:05.884
metal leg coverings.

45
00:03:09.586 --> 00:03:11.606
She picked up the helmet and almost dropped it.

46
00:03:11.626 --> 00:03:14.468
"Wow," she said.

47
00:03:14.488 --> 00:03:16.048
"This stuff is heavy!"

48
00:03:16.068 --> 00:03:18.109
"No kidding."

49
00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:20.690
Brody put on one of the leg coverings.

50
00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.072
"This gear is a lot heavier than my football pads.

51
00:03:25.764 --> 00:03:28.426
It's not going to be easy to run in all this stuff."

52
00:03:28.446 --> 00:03:31.648
"Don't forget this."

53
00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:33.750
Markos picked up the shield.

54
00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.794
"Be careful not to drop it while you're running, or you'll have to stop and retrieve it.

55
00:03:39.274 --> 00:03:40.355
That will slow you down."

56
00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:44.097
"Okay. Hold the shield while I put on my helmet."

57
00:03:46.079 --> 00:03:48.340
Brody adjusted the metal helmet on his head.

58
00:03:48.941 --> 00:03:50.882
Then he took the shield from Markos.

59
00:03:50.902 --> 00:03:53.084
"Ready, boy?"

60
00:03:53.568 --> 00:03:55.830
Hermes stepped forward, looking impatient.

61
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.432
"Athena's champion is waiting."

62
00:03:59.753 --> 00:04:00.254
"I'm ready."

63
00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.516
Brody took a few steps toward the other athlete.

64
00:04:04.317 --> 00:04:06.459
His armor clanked with every step.

65
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.643
As soon as Brody neared Athena's champion, the goddess waved her hand.

66
00:04:11.663 --> 00:04:16.167
"Go!" Athena's champion started running.

67
00:04:16.187 --> 00:04:18.369
Brody looked startled.

68
00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:20.591
"Hey!" he exclaimed.

69
00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:21.832
"I wasn't ready!"

70
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.061
He lurched forward.

71
00:04:24.621 --> 00:04:27.982
The armor on one of his legs caught on the armor on the other leg.

72
00:04:28.002 --> 00:04:30.163
"Brody, look out!"

73
00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:31.524
Julia cried.

74
00:04:32.664 --> 00:04:33.604
It was too late.

75
00:04:33.624 --> 00:04:35.345
Brody tripped and fell.

76
00:04:36.706 --> 00:04:41.287
His shield went flying as he hit the ground with a clank and a loud "oof!"

77
00:04:44.029 --> 00:04:46.510
"Stop!" Athena called to her champion.

78
00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.230
"We need to start over."

79
00:04:49.191 --> 00:04:52.312
Julia and Markos ran over to help Brody to his feet.

80
00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.441
"Are you all right?"

81
00:04:55.041 --> 00:04:55.862
Markos asked.

82
00:04:55.882 --> 00:04:57.403
"Did you hurt yourself?"

83
00:04:59.644 --> 00:05:00.765
"I don't think so."

84
00:05:01.365 --> 00:05:04.087
Brody took a few steps and then made a face.

85
00:05:04.107 --> 00:05:06.889
"But this is ridiculous.

86
00:05:07.489 --> 00:05:09.231
How am I supposed to run like this?

87
00:05:10.131 --> 00:05:12.513
Especially here, in this crowded space."

88
00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:15.475
Julia was surprised.

89
00:05:15.955 --> 00:05:18.757
She'd never heard Brody express doubt before.

90
00:05:20.098 --> 00:05:23.040
Usually he acted so confident—too confident!

91
00:05:24.284 --> 00:05:25.504
Then he looked over at her.

92
00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.545
"Sorry," he said.

93
00:05:27.565 --> 00:05:31.406
"I mean, I know you're counting on me to get us home.

94
00:05:32.006 --> 00:05:33.727
I just hope I can really do it."

95
00:05:34.827 --> 00:05:36.647
"You will," Julia said.

96
00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.408
"You can do this, Brody.

97
00:05:39.448 --> 00:05:42.369
You learned how to throw the javelin and the discus, remember?"

98
00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:44.850
"That's different."

99
00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.150
Brody frowned and kicked at the shield on the ground.

100
00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:53.612
"It will be easier when you're running in the Olympic stadium," Julia said.

101
00:05:54.892 --> 00:05:57.613
"For now, you just have to focus, and you'll be fine.

102
00:05:58.013 --> 00:06:00.294
You have lots of natural athletic ability."

103
00:06:00.314 --> 00:06:02.295
"Do you really think so?"

104
00:06:02.755 --> 00:06:03.796
Brody blinked at her.

105
00:06:04.476 --> 00:06:06.457
Then slowly he smiled.

106
00:06:06.477 --> 00:06:08.938
"Maybe you're right.

107
00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:11.339
I'm the best football player on my team.

108
00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:13.360
Coach says I can do anything!"

109
00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.741
He grabbed his shield again.

110
00:06:16.721 --> 00:06:19.883
By then Athena's champion had returned to the starting line.

111
00:06:19.903 --> 00:06:21.743
"Ready, boy?"

112
00:06:22.204 --> 00:06:23.004
Hermes asked.

113
00:06:23.976 --> 00:06:27.639
Brody smacked his shield with his free hand, making it clang.

114
00:06:27.659 --> 00:06:29.861
"Ready!" he cried.

115
00:06:29.881 --> 00:06:33.584
"Do you really think he can do this?"

116
00:06:34.465 --> 00:06:38.248
Markos asked Julia quietly as the two athletes lined up again.

117
00:06:39.329 --> 00:06:40.210
Julia shrugged.

118
00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.431
"I guess we're about to find out."

119
00:06:42.451 --> 00:06:45.574
"Go!" Athena said.

120
00:06:46.735 --> 00:06:50.478
This time Brody and the other champion leaped forward together.

121
00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:54.885
After a few steps, Athena's champion pulled ahead.

122
00:06:54.905 --> 00:06:57.186
"Go, Brody!"

123
00:06:57.707 --> 00:06:58.587
Julia yelled.

124
00:06:58.607 --> 00:07:00.088
"You can do it!"

125
00:07:04.551 --> 00:07:10.574
After another few steps, Brody surged forward, catching up to, and then passing, the other runner.

126
00:07:10.594 --> 00:07:13.356
"Why is he holding his shield like that?"

127
00:07:13.836 --> 00:07:14.676
Markos asked.

128
00:07:14.696 --> 00:07:17.018
"He's cradling it like a baby."

129
00:07:18.398 --> 00:07:20.800
For a second Julia couldn't figure it out either.

130
00:07:22.092 --> 00:07:24.194
Then she realized what Brody was doing.

131
00:07:24.214 --> 00:07:28.117
"He's pretending it's a football!"

132
00:07:28.677 --> 00:07:29.858
she said with a smile.

133
00:07:29.878 --> 00:07:33.101
"That probably makes him feel more confident."

134
00:07:34.502 --> 00:07:37.044
Hermes' cheers suddenly filled the air.

135
00:07:40.147 --> 00:07:44.770
Julia cheered too as Brody crossed the line well ahead of the other runner.

136
00:07:45.551 --> 00:07:46.392
He'd done it!
